      "name": "REMBI: Recommended Metadata for Biological Images",
      "description": "Guidelines/draft metadata standard for biological imaging (light, electron and X‑ray microscopy). Specifies recommended metadata elements to describe samples, image-acquisition parameters, experimental context, processing, and provenance to support archiving, discovery and reuse of microscopy data (FAIR-oriented); intended for adoption by archives (e.g. BioImage Archive, EMPIAR, Cell‑IDR, Tissue‑IDR) and community implementation."
